## DEFECT-2 (harness, this seat) — runner crash on [3/3]

/tmp/kengaku-r19-devin/run_p4_seat.py:180 raised NameError: name 'rec' is not
defined after the 8791 stream had fully completed (stale rec[...] writes left in
the stream branch from an earlier patch round). Consequence: the receipt line for
[3/3] says "http=error" though the HTTP exchange itself was 200 (journal + captured
usage/headers prove it). The response data in the receipt is the data the shim
returned; only the status label is wrong. Recorded, not patched in place; the
corrected status is carried in this addendum with the journal rid as evidence.
Request accounting for this seat: 3 seat requests (8787) + 3 P4 requests
(2 x 8793, 1 x 8791) = 6 total; battery budget share: P4(i) warm-up + P4(i) +
P4(ii) = 3 of the battery's 18 (within budget; the duplicate warm-up was the
crash-retry of [1/3] after the first harness crash, logged as [1/3] twice).

## DEFECT-3 (battery-design, filed for the scorer) — frozen P4 body is unservable

plans/probe-battery-r19.md:170-171 freezes `"temperature":0` in the P4 body. The
devin leg (leg 2 of the live glm-flash shim) refuses temperature:0 with 400
invalid_argument (M10 found the same on opus; my seat D2 found it on swe-2 —
the refusal is shim/upstream-wide, not model-specific). The battery's own §3
clause ("If a lane 400s naming stream_options, record that as the outcome...
no reshaped retry") anticipated a stream_options refusal; the actual refusal is
temperature. Either way: frozen body -> no measurement. The battery's P4
prediction (4a point 11734) was calibrated on the r18 census body, which used
the SAME temperature:0 shape but reached the devin leg as leg 1 directly
(pre-M9 order). Under the live zai-first order the request reaches devin only
after a zai 429, and the devin leg's 400 is terminal — the r18 measurement
path no longer exists on this shim.

